id: pm-gh1368
title: "GH-1368: Agent UX: context next silently ignores inherited --fields and --depth options, including invalid values"
description: "Reported agent-facing contract defect imported from https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1368. Preserve existing shipped foundations. Detailed source observations are dated 2026-09-30 and must be revalidated before implementation."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: gh-1368,github-intake,sdk-first
created_at: "2026-10-02T17:09:29.485Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-03T12:45:09.089Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-03T12:45:08.463Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-03T12:45:08.463Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "An id/title/description projection returns the requested stored description and documented mandatory metadata, or is explicitly rejected as unsupported; Unknown fields and invalid depth return nonzero typed errors; Parent flag placement and aliases do not change validation; Recommended and companion rows follow one documented projection rule; Tests cover other inherited controls to catch accepted-but-unused flags; No regression to next ranking, blocker visibility or token-budget enforcement"
parent: pm-4k6b
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "Namespaced leaves reject undeclared ancestor options before host preparation, forward only compatible supplied controls and preserve explicit leaf precedence. Lightweight command selection consumes published SDK option arity so ordinary command-like option values do not expand registration. The exact CLI refusal census includes this transport grammar boundary and the real literal-tag regression protects minimal family registration."
expected_result: "Context next applies and validates supported inherited projection and depth controls, or rejects unsupported controls with a typed actionable error before execution; invalid values cannot silently succeed."
actual_result: "Final corrected-source isolated suite: 9638 passed and two Windows-only cases skipped on Linux; exact coverage 100/100/100/100 with zero uncovered counts (66545/66545 statements, 50900/50900 branches, 13748/13748 functions, 63447/63447 lines). Full type checking, every static-quality stage including unchanged performance ceilings, graph/history and mutation controls (329 killed, seven reviewed equivalent, zero failures), native deduplicated linked tests, 58 clean packed Node/Bun manual commands with history verification, and nine npx/bunx packed package workflows plus typed SDK consumers passed. All 28 touched source functions have behavior-specific documentation. Required Sentry/telemetry gate passed with zero blocking issues, 1.40 percent finish error rate and zero missing error-code rows. Earlier failed test/coverage and performance observations remain recorded. Exact-head hosted checks/reviews and merge follow through PR1376; this batch is separate from the earlier v2026.10.3 publication and four pre-existing-main nightly alerts."
